-- and the chiral solvating agent. The molecule is 1-(9-anthryl)-2,2,2-trifluoroethanol, Pirkle's alcohol;
-- what the admission test asks of it is only that no improper operation is among its symmetries, which is
-- what being chiral is, so it is written here with its trifluoromethyl rotation and nothing improper.
-- Atoms 0 to 3 are that carbon and its three fluorines; none of them is counted, since the agent's own
-- resonances are not the measurement.
sp-pirkle : Species
sp-pirkle = (4 , cons (nat-cyc (cons 1 (cons 2 (cons 3 nil))) , srate-flat 12 , true) nil , nil)
